> doing this).
>
> So to summarize, yes it looks like the cigar utils in GenomicRanges
> can safely ignore the P operations. I'll do that change.

Done in GenomicRanges 1.7.33 (latest devel version). With this version:

   > library(GenomicRanges)
   > cig1 <- "6M1P4M2D5M20N3I2M"
   > cig2 <- "10M2D5M20N3I2M"
   > cigarToIRanges(cig1)
   IRanges of length 2
       start end width
   [1]     1  17    17
   [2]    38  39     2
   > cigarToIRanges(cig2)
   IRanges of length 2
       start end width
   [1]     1  17    17
   [2]    38  39     2
   > cigarToQWidth(cig1)
   [1] 20
   > cigarToQWidth(cig2)
   [1] 20

The "silent deletion from padded reference" is ignored by the 2 central
low-level cigar utils cigarToIRanges() and cigarToQWidth(). All the
other cigar utils and higher level operations like coercion from
GappedAlignment to GRanges or GRangesList behave consistently with
this.

GenomicRanges 1.7.33 will become available via BiocInstaller::biocLite()
and to R 2.15 users only in the next 24 hours.

Cheers,
H.

